ample, not independent forecasting validation. Non-overlap observations use a fixed calendar anchor. Effective information is much smaller than the daily n when returns overlap.</small></p></details>
<details open><summary>Regimes · subsequent 20-session total returns</summary><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>CNN band</th><th>n overlapping days</th><th>SPY mean</th><th>SPY vs all days / CI</th><th>QQQ mean</th><th>QQQ vs all days / CI</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Extreme fear (0–25)</td><td>189</td><td>2.75%</td><td>+1.59 pp<br><small>[-0.52, 3.39]</small></td><td>3.07%</td><td>+1.73 pp<br><small>[-0.88, 4.14]</small></td></tr><tr><td>Fear (>25–<45)</td><td>445</td><td>1.28%</td><td>+0.11 pp<br><small>[-0.70, 0.89]</small></td><td>1.27%</td><td>-0.08 pp<br><small>[-1.17, 0.98]</small></td></tr><tr><td>Neutral (45–55)</td><td>227</td><td>0.18%</td><td>-0.99 pp<br><small>[-1.96, -0.13]</small></td><td>0.15%</td><td>-1.19 pp<br><small>[-2.52, 0.02]</small></td></tr><tr><td>Greed (>55–<75)</td><td>457</td><td>0.87%</td><td>-0.30 pp<br><small>[-1.16, 0.53]</small></td><td>1.36%</td><td>+0.01 pp<br><small>[-1.22, 1.29]</small></td></tr><tr><td>Extreme greed (75–100)</td><td>80</td><td>1.31%</td><td>+0.14 pp<br><small>[-1.98, 1.68]</small></td><td>1.00%</td><td>-0.35 pp<br><small>[-3.05, 1.89]</small></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Unconditional means over the same eligible observations: SPY <b>1.17%</b>; QQQ <b>1.34%</b>. Extreme-fear averages are higher, but their incremental-return intervals include zero. Extreme greed did not imply negative average returns. Bands were fixed in advance of calculation; n counts days, not distinct fear episodes.</p></details>
<details><summary>Stability across years and chronological periods</summary><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>SPY same-day</th><th>QQQ same-day</th><th>SPY forward 20d</th><th>QQQ forward 20d</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2021</td><td>0.77</td><td>0.65</td><td>-0.32</td><td>-0.39</td></tr><tr><td>2022</td><td>0.64</td><td>0.64</td><td>-0.39</td><td>-0.40</td></tr><tr><td>2023</td><td>0.64</td><td>0.52</td><td>-0.32</td><td>-0.25</td></tr><tr><td>2024</td><td>0.66</td><td>0.63</td><td>-0.16</td><td>-0.12</td></tr><tr><td>2025</td><td>0.53</td><td>0.55</td><td>0.09</td><td>0.07</td></tr><tr><td>2026</td><td>0.78</td><td>0.71</td><td>-0.37</td><td>-0.23</td></tr></tbody></table><table><thead><tr><th>ETF</th><th>Period</th><th>n</th><th>Forward 20d r</th><th>95% interval</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>SPY</td><td>2021–2024</td><td>965</td><td>-0.16</td><td>[-0.36, 0.02]</td></tr><tr><td>SPY</td><td>2025–2026</td><td>412</td><td>-0.06</td><td>[-0.42, 0.36]</td></tr><tr><td>QQQ</td><td>2021–2024</td><td>965</td><td>-0.11</td><td>[-0.29, 0.06]</td></tr><tr><td>QQQ</td><td>2025–2026</td><td>412</td><td>-0.04</td><td>[-0.39, 0.41]</td></tr><tr><td>QQQ/SPY</td><td>2021–2024</td><td>965</td><td>0.00</td><td>[-0.16, 0.18]</td></tr><tr><td>QQQ/SPY</td><td>2025–2026</td><td>412</td><td>0.03</td><td>[-0.27, 0.38]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Forward outcomes crossing each period/year boundary are excluded. The 2025 forward relationship changed sign; the pooled 2025–2026 relationship is near zero. This is a chronological robustness check, not an untouched live holdout.</p></details>
<details><summary>Sources, alignment and limitations</summary><p><a href="https://www.cnn.com/markets/fear-and-greed">CNN official methodology</a>: seven equally weighted market indicators, including S&amp;P 500 relative to its 125-day average and stocks versus bonds over 20 sessions. <a href="https://production.dataviz.cnn.io/index/fearandgreed/graphdata/2026-09-18">Official CNN historical endpoint</a>. ETF returns: Bloomberg Desktop API, gross dividend-reinvested total-return indices.</p><p>Pearson and Spearman; primary predictive entry is next-session close, then +1/+5/+20/+60 ETF sessions. Same-day correlation is not predictive. Circular moving-block bootstrap, 500 repetitions, block=max(20,horizon). Separate years and 2021–2024 / 2025–2026 windows; no threshold optimization. One CNN date is missing (2026-03-12); it remains missing. The duplicated latest-day observation was resolved by timestamp. Historical UTC-midnight stamps are treated as date labels, not shifted to the preceding US date.</p><ul><li>CNN is partly constructed from stock momentum, breadth, volatility and stocks-versus-bonds; same-day association is endogenous.</li><li>Retrospectively downloaded, potentially revised history; immutable publication-time CNN vintages are unavailable.</li><li>Current day excluded from the historical study even after regular close; latest CNN displayed separately.</li><li>Price-level correlation can be misleading because prices trend while the index is bounded. It is diagnostic only.</li><li>Overlapping forward returns reduce independent observations; block intervals and non-overlapping checks are provided.</li><li>Multiple horizons and regimes are exploratory; confidence intervals are not adjusted for multiple testing.</li><li>QQQ/SPY means the ratio of gross total-return indices (relative performance), not the P&amp;L of a dollar-neutral long/short portfolio.</li><li>No transaction costs, trading strategy or causal claim. Sample starts February 2021 and excludes the 2020 crash.</li></ul><p>Missing values are never filled with zero; current-day CNN is shown only as context. Local raw snapshots, date-level calculations and input hashes are retained for audit.</p></details></section></details></main></html>